<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed Belkadi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1527</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ahmed ibn al-Qadi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed Belkadi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cabyle">Kabyle</a> leader from a family of judges who founded the Kingdom of Kuku in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djurdjura">Djurdjura</a> mountains around 1515. Allying at first with the Barbarossa brothers and then turning against them, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Hayreddin Barbarossa</a> in 1520 and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> for several years until Hayreddin retook it and he was killed in 1527.</p></div>
